WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.389
So Donald Trump really may not need to steal
this election.

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:08.040
We actually have the latest 538 projection
which says that there's a 71 percent chance

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.910
Joe Biden wins and a 29 percent chance Donald
Trump wins.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.040
You might recall those are very similar numbers
to 2016.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.170
And in 2016, of course, it went the way of
the 29 percent.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.610
So we're going to deal with that tomorrow.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:26.560
But the point is, Trump may not need to steal
the election, but he's not taking any chances

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.560
and he's going to try to steal it.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.560
Because why not?

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.690
If you can do it, why wouldn't you do it now
without redoing my previous commentary on

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.420
the race being closer than these double digit
polling lead suggest?

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:45.670
I'll remind you when Joe Biden is up nine
in a poll with a three point five margin of

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:46.760
error.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.469
That means Joe Biden might only be up to in
the popular vote with the popular vote win

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:55.309
of two point two in 2016.

00:00:55.309 --> 00:00:58.820
Hillary lost, so I won't redo the entire commentary.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:04.010
But but the point is, when we see these leads
for Joe Biden, we just we really have to assume

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.010
nothing.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.869
And in fact, the 538 forecast, which I'll
go over in detail with you tomorrow, supports

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.479
this very, very closely.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:16.119
But what we should know is this is going to
be an election that if Trump can steal it,

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:17.210
he's going to try to steal it.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.789
And we need to understand all of the ways
in which he's going to try to do that.

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:25.749
Up first of all, Donald Trump has been saying,
oh, this is going to be an unfair election.

00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:27.319
He's trying to make it unfair.

00:01:27.319 --> 00:01:29.799
Donald Trump has been saying this election
will be rigged.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:32.359
Well, he's the one trying to rig it.

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:35.049
Trump has been saying vote by mail won't be
reliable.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:39.189
He's the one trying to make it unreliable
by kneecapping the post office.

00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:45.239
And Ryan Cooper wrote a good piece this week
in the week in the publication The Week called

00:01:45.239 --> 00:01:48.539
Donald Trump is trying to steal the election.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:53.929
And he outlines the various tactics and strategies
and approaches that Donald Trump is employing.

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:55.950
And there's actually a lot of them.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.380
And whether we can fight all of them at once
or how we do it is sort of the next question.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.770
But we've mentioned some of these before,
and I want to put them together in a list.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.000
So, first of all, I mentioned this already.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.069
Donald Trump is trying to break the post office.

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:14.739
The idea is if people are going to vote by
mail, if states are going to expand absentee

00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:20.890
ballot access, break the post office so that
it will be less likely to succeed in polls.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:25.750
We've looked at Trump supporters among those
planning to vote in person.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.969
Two thirds are Trump voters, among those planning
to vote by mail.

00:02:29.969 --> 00:02:32.510
Almost three quarters are Biden voters.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:36.690
So you see right away why Trump would try
to break the post office.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.090
That's one strategy.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:46.420
Number two, Donald Trump is trying to fine
tune and find time a stimulus, a second stimulus

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:52.040
so that it will be best positioned to essentially
buy votes.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:58.910
And part of this is that Donald Trump has
said I will defer payroll taxes if he can

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.269
write what, we'll see if he can actually do
it.

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:06.620
And if you reelect me, I will make the deferral
a permanent cut.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:13.749
Okay, so he's effectively saying I will defer
your payroll taxes for now, but unless you

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:21.550
reelect me when you file your taxes next year
for this calendar year 2020, you will owe

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.950
the money you saved on the payroll tax.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:30.590
But if you reelect me, I will make the deferral
a forgiveness if it's trying to buy votes.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:36.060
The right loves to say, oh, Bernie's trying
to buy votes with free stuff like health care,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.600
which would be paid for through taxes.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.470
This is really trying to buy votes, saying,
I'll defer, I'll save you some money for now.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:48.349
You're going to owe it back in aped by April
15th of 2021, unless you reelect me.

00:03:48.349 --> 00:03:49.349
Okay.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:50.349
Trying to buy votes.

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:58.620
Number three, Donald Trump is trying to delegitimize
the election to weaponize his followers, taking

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.739
to the streets after November 3rd.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:02.920
And it is working.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.090
We have a new poll which shows that two thirds
of Republican voters now believe that the

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.099
election may not be fair.

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:14.859
I'm going to talk about that later in its
own segment because it's so important and

00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:18.699
in such a big deal and really is the goal
of all of this.

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:23.560
Donald Trump is using lawsuits to try to turn
the courts.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.520
Remember that the courts, one of the biggest
successes, if you can call it that, one of

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:33.530
the biggest accomplishments of the Trump administration
is mostly thanks to Mitch McConnell's help

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.300
getting to Supreme Court justices confirmed,
one of which should have been d'Hondt of Barack

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:44.919
Obama's selection, Merrick Garland and getting
hundreds of lower court judges confirmed.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:48.381
So Donald Trump is using lawsuits and he's
being open about it.

00:04:48.381 --> 00:04:50.180
He's talking about we've got this in court.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.650
We've got that in court.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:59.229
He's trying to use lawsuits to turn the courts
in his favor after the alleged.

00:04:59.229 --> 00:05:02.110
Sean, and to try to prevent vote by mail.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.710
So there's two two sides to this.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:09.590
Use the courts now to try to block vote by
mail in different states and start laying

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:14.560
the groundwork to if there's a challenge after
the election.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.840
Have courts that maybe will be more predisposed
to rule in Donald Trump's favor.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:22.840
And you might remember that for a couple weeks
now, Donald Trump has been warning it could

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:23.840
take days.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.069
It could take weeks, it could take months.

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:28.580
Trump even said it could take years to know
who won the November election.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.639
That's not going to happen.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:35.620
But the point is, Trump is trying to ensure
that it takes longer than it has to.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:41.160
With the lawsuits, with the destruction of
the postal service, so on and so forth.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.060
Now, again, Trump might not need to do this
stuff.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:50.740
Trump might be able to win without suppressing
the vote, without turning to fraud.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:56.599
But it's possible that the only way Trump
can win is with these tactics.

00:05:56.599 --> 00:06:00.990
And this very well could end up being the
craziest presidential election that the U.S.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.930
will have ever had, at least in the modern
political era.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.289
So what do we do?

00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:06.289
Come on.

00:06:06.289 --> 00:06:07.289
You guys know what we do.

00:06:07.289 --> 00:06:08.289
You know what we do?

00:06:08.289 --> 00:06:09.319
We vote early.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:12.300
Ideally, they can slow down your ballot.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:16.229
Trump can slow down your ballot by having
Lewis the joy.

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:21.720
The new postmaster general who is a Trump
donor, restrict overtime so that mail piles

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.199
up in post offices.

00:06:24.199 --> 00:06:30.050
Look at trying to shut down some postal offices,
post offices or whatever.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.979
But if you mail in your ballot three weeks
early, even if it's slowed down by one, two,

00:06:34.979 --> 00:06:37.009
three, four days, it's going to get there.

00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:40.629
And presumably, presumably, it's going to
be counted unless Trump figures out a way

00:06:40.629 --> 00:06:44.970
to mess with the actual election and voting
precincts themselves.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.069
They can close polling places.

00:06:47.069 --> 00:06:52.250
But if you plan to vote early, you will be
less affected by that.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:56.569
So put the mask on or do the Maylin thing
or whatever.

00:06:56.569 --> 00:06:57.569
Let's do this.

00:06:57.569 --> 00:07:02.669
We know now that it is Biden and Harris could
not be more different than Trump and Pence

00:07:02.669 --> 00:07:06.580
for all of the complaints we might have about
a lack of perfection in this ticket.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.660
And certainly there are many.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:13.500
And be aware of when and where you can start
to vote early.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.010
I'm going to talk about that a little bit
in the next segment.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:31.189
But a lot that we

00:07:31.189 --> 00:07:52.150
can

00:07:52.150 --> 00:08:13.819
do

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:32.169
and a lot that we should be doing,

